# Copy to .env. Everything with the EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix is INLINED INTO THE
# BUNDLE at build time — it ships to every device and is readable by anyone
# who downloads the app. An OAuth client id is fine there (it is public by
# design); a secret of any kind is not, and never goes in this file.

# ---- where the API lives ---------------------------------------------------
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://grail-market-backend.onrender.com
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SCAN_URL=https://grailmarket.duckdns.org

# ---- Sign in with Google ---------------------------------------------------
# From Google Cloud console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials. One per
# platform; they are not interchangeable.
#
# The iOS one is also read by app.config.ts, which turns it into the reversed
# URL scheme the OAuth redirect comes back on. Change it and rebuild, or the
# redirect arrives at a scheme the app does not answer.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
